# Build context of infra/docker/{api,dashboard,flow,code-runner}.Dockerfile (the repository root; Phase 11,
# Workflow 11C), and vision's named context `repo`, from which it copies two files. services/vision has its
# own context and .dockerignore.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
.git
# Docker's patterns are rooted, unlike .gitignore's: a bare `.env.*` would miss e2e/.env.e2e.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
android
services
models
# C46.1: the web flow runs YuNet in the browser; its build copies the model (C48, review F10)
# and checks it against its pin in the manifest (infra/tests/apps-image-context.test.sh).
!models/face_detection_yunet_2026may.onnx
!models/manifest.json
data
# Phase 5 (C56, C61.5, C67, F15): the API reads these data files at run time. The disposable list
# comes from python3 scripts/fetch_data.py; data/raw and other downloads stay out.
!data/manifest.json
!data/malicious-feeds.json
!data/disposable_email_blocklist.conf
# Phase 6 (C78.3, F14): the filtered variant groups the worker, seed:dev and the watchlist CLIs
# load, built by `pnpm --filter @openverify/watchlist build:variant-groups` after fetch_data.py.
# The unfiltered rigour file it is built from stays out (ADR 0005: only the filtered file ships).
!data/variant-groups.json
# Workflow 7A (C92.6): the pinned hosting and VPN ASN seeds (scripts/fetch_data.py), which the network
# facts read. ADR 0006: no live network data and no operator anonymous-IP file enters the image;
# data/ip-reputation is mounted read-only by compose instead.
!data/x4bnet-datacenter-ASN.txt
!data/x4bnet-vpn-ASN.txt
!data/bad-asn-list.csv
**/*.mmdb
**/*.mmdb.gz
fixtures/faces
fixtures/generated
e2e/.artifacts
